            <ArticleTitle>Population-averaged and cluster-specific models for clustered ordinal response data.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2573-88</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We compare population-averaged and cluster-specific models for clustered ordinal data. We consider generalized estimating equations and constrained equations maximum likelihood estimation of population-averaged cumulative logit regression models, and mixed effects estimation of cluster-specific cumulative logit regression models. A previously reported relationship between population-averaged and cluster-specific parameters for the binary logistic link appears to hold for analogous parameters under the cumulative logit link. We address these issues in the context of data from two cross-over clinical trials.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
